review_issues.problem:
Several mandatory elements and scope items rest on capacity that is entirely absent from the dossier:
- no SSH expertise (ME3, SC5);
- no producer, logistics, retailer or authority involvement (ME2; F25 confirms none);
- no pathogen-handling facility (SC1, EO2);
- no field or commercial deployment for a TRL 6 end point;
- no EU coordination experience.
The call is achievable only by proposing several new partners as planned. That is a stretch task, not a close fit, and mislabelling it distorts difficulty calibration.

Several limitations that a proposal must address are not in the registry:
- no SSH researcher or expertise in any partner (ME3);
- no recorded contact or role for food safety authorities (ME2);
- no facility or permission for pathogen work beyond the CL1 surrogate rooms;
- 'Current allocations are committed to the activities specified in their respective award records' (no spare existing capacity).
F02 is also categorised as 'grant', although it is mostly a publication and supervision record.
